    "a or an for kids",
    "when to use an",
    "english grammar for kids",
    "kids learning"
  ],
  "cast": [
    "LEO",
    "MIA"
  ],
  "loop_card": {
    "text": "A or an?",
    "cue": "next",
    "left": "🍎",
    "right": "⚽"
  },
  "lines": [
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, why do we say \"an apple\" but \"a ball\"?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "🍎",
          "label": "An apple"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "⚽",
          "label": "A ball"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It's all about the next sound! We use \"an\" before a vowel sound, and \"a\" before a consonant sound.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👂",
        "text": "Listen to the next sound",
        "cue": "next",
        "sub": "an + vowel sound",
        "sub_cue": "vowel"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why does it matter?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Try saying \"a apple\". Your words bump together! \"An apple\" is much smoother.",
      "punch": "smoother",
      "board": {
        "type": "transform",
        "title": "Smooth it out",
        "from": {
          "icon": "😖",
          "label": "a apple",
          "cue": "try"
        },
        "to": {
          "icon": "🍎",
          "label": "an apple",
          "cue": "smoother"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So how do I pick?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "First, look at the next word. Then listen to its first sound. Finally, pick \"a\" or \"an\".",
      "board": {
        "type": "flow",
        "title": "Pick a or an",
        "packet": "🔤",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "👀",
            "label": "Look at word",
            "cue": "look"
          },
          {
            "icon": "👂",
            "label": "Hear first sound",
            "cue": "listen"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✅",
            "label": "Pick a or an",
            "cue": "pick"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Like \"an egg\" and \"a dog\"?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! \"An egg\", \"an owl\", \"an umbrella\". But \"a dog\", \"a cat\", \"a tree\".",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "An",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🥚",
              "text": "egg",
              "cue": "egg"
            },
            {
              "icon": "🦉",
              "text": "owl",
              "cue": "owl"
            },
            {
              "icon": "☂️",
              "text": "umbrella",
              "cue": "umbrella"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "A",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🐶",
              "text": "dog",
              "cue": "dog"
            },
            {
              "icon": "🐱",
              "text": "cat",
              "cue": "cat"
            },
            {
              "icon": "🌳",
              "text": "tree",
              "cue": "tree"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What about \"hour\"? It starts with H!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "The H in \"hour\" is silent, so it starts with a vowel sound. We say \"an hour\"!",
      "punch": "silent",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⏰",
        "text": "An hour",
        "cue": "hour",
        "sub": "Silent H!",
        "sub_cue": "silent"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "\"Unicorn\" starts with U. That's a vowel!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Tricky! \"Unicorn\" starts with a \"you\" sound. That's a consonant sound, so it's \"a unicorn\".",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🦄",
        "text": "A unicorn",
        "cue": "unicorn",
        "sub": "Starts with \"you\"",
        "sub_cue": "starts"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "An apple, an hour, a ball, a unicorn!",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
          {
            "text": "an apple",
            "icon": "🍎",
            "cue": "apple"
          },
          {
            "text": "an hour",
            "icon": "⏰",
            "cue": "hour"
          },
          {
            "text": "a ball",
            "icon": "⚽",
            "cue": "ball"
          },
          {
            "text": "a unicorn",
            "icon": "🦄",
            "cue": "unicorn"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What should we find out next? Ask a grown-up to drop a topic in the comment section!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Exactly! Follow the sound, not the letter. Ask a grown-up to subscribe to The Curio Kids Club for more wonders, and share this with a friend! And next time someone asks... why do we say \"an apple\" but \"a ball\"?"
